What it is for: databases, admin panels and internal services that must
not be public

Why it helps: `sshr tunnel prod db` instead of remembering `-L
5432:localhost:5432`, `-R` for webhooks and showing a local dev server,
`-D` as a SOCKS proxy

Why this way: `ExitOnForwardFailure` makes a busy port fail at once, and
a stopped sshr stops its ssh too, so no tunnel is left holding a port
